"要ラヌワ・・・\n"
"シマッテオケ。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:1
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#1"
msgid ""
"ソレ、イラナイ。\n"
"オレニハ、イラナイ。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:2
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#2"
msgid ""
"我には要り用のない物。\n"
"もとに収めておくがよろし。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:3
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#3"
msgid ""
"ふむ、文字通りつまらないものですね。\n"
"私は遠慮させていただきましょう。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:4
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#4"
msgid ""
"わたくしに、まさかそのような不粋な物が\n"
"似合うと、お思いではないでしょうね。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:5
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#5"
msgid "なんだよそれ、要らねえよそんなもん。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:6
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#6"
msgid "なにそれー、あんたバカじゃないの？"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:7
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#7"
msgid ""
"子供を物でつるつもりなの？\n"
"まったく大人ってのは・・・。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:8
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#8"
msgid "おじちゃん、あたし、そんなの要らない。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:9
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#9"
msgid ""
"まあ、嬉しい。\n"
"でも、気持ちだけ頂くことにするわね。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:10
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#10"
msgid ""
"えへへへへ、いいもんくれんじゃねえか。\n"
"さっそく捨ててやるよ。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:11
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#11"
msgid ""
"ふぉっふぉっふぉっ、\n"
"そいつは、わしには不用のものじゃのう。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:12
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#12"
msgid ""
"キミ、ゴミはくずかごに捨てたまえ。\n"
"そんなもの渡されても困るんだよ。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:13
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#13"
msgid ""
"そんなしょーもないもん、いるか！\n"
"もっとましなもん、持ってこい。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:14
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#14"
msgid ""
"ヌルヌル？\n"
"ズーズーズズー・・・。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#. Same Japanese also at: COMBDATA/BOSSTALK.EVE#14, BUTU_SRF.MDT#51, BUTU_SRF.MDT#87, BUTU_SRF.MDT#123.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:15
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#15"
msgid "・・・・・・・・。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:36
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#36"
msgid "フム、モラオウカ。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:37
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#37"
msgid "ソレ、モラウゾ。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:38
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#38"
msgid ""
"特に要り用の物ではないが、\n"
"収めておくことにするぞえ。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:39
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#39"
msgid ""
"貴殿からの贈り物、\n"
"有難く、頂くことにしよう。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:40
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#40"
msgid "今回は、これで我慢してあげますわ。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:41
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#41"
msgid ""
"それ、俺にくれるのか？\n"
"まあ、もらっといてやるよ。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:42
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#42"
msgid ""
"ちょっとぉ、他に何かないわけ？\n"
"まあ、仕方ないわね、もらってあげるわ。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:43
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#43"
msgid ""
"ありがとう、おじさん。\n"
"子供は素直に受け取らなきゃね。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:44
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#44"
msgid ""
"あたし、つまんなくても、物って大好き。\n"
"おじちゃん、ありがとね。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:45
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#45"
msgid ""
"まあ、嬉しい。\n"
"次はもっと、いいものくれるんでしょう？"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:46
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#46"
msgid ""
"そんなの要らねえよ。\n"
"もっとくれ。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:47
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#47"
msgid ""
"豊かなことは、ええことじゃのう。\n"
"頂くぞい。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:48
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#48"
msgid ""
"どうしてもと言うのでしたら、\n"
"仕方ない、引き取ってあげましょう。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:49
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#49"
msgid ""
"まぁそんぐらいで、まけといたろか。\n"
"おおきに。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:50
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#50"
msgid ""
"ピチャッピチャッ、\n"
"ズズー・・・。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#. Same Japanese also at: COMBDATA/BOSSTALK.EVE#14, BUTU_SRF.MDT#15, BUTU_SRF.MDT#87, BUTU_SRF.MDT#123.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:51
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#51"
msgid "・・・・・・・・。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:72
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#72"
msgid ""
"ツネヅネ、嬉シイコトヲ、シテクレル。\n"
"人間ニ、シテオクニハ、モッタイナイナ。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:73
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#73"
msgid ""
"オレ、ウレシイ。スゴク、ウレシイ。\n"
"コンゴトモ、ヨロシク。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:74
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#74"
msgid ""
"我らのきずな、\n"
"より堅固に結ばれていく。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:75
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#75"
msgid ""
"貴殿に忠誠を誓う時も、\n"
"そう遠くはないだろう。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:76
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#76"
msgid ""
"そんなに私のことが気になりますの？\n"
"今夜、つきあってあげてもよくってよ。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:77
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#77"
msgid ""
"忠誠度アーップ！\n"
"＞俺の気持ちが上がった。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:78
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#78"
msgid ""
"あたし・・・、いつかきっと、\n"
"あなたのモノになったげる。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:79
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#79"
msgid ""
"へえ、ボクの欲しい物よくわかるね。\n"
"おじさん、いいとこあるじゃん。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:80
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#80"
msgid ""
"ねぇ、おじちゃんって、\n"
"なんでこんなに優しいの。アリガトウ。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:81
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#81"
msgid ""
"あら素敵！プレゼントって、\n"
"幾つになっても、嬉しいものなのよね。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:82
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#82"
msgid ""
"ふざけんじゃねえぞ、コラ！\n"
"スゲエ、嬉しいじゃねえか。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:83
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#83"
msgid ""
"先の短い年寄りには、もったいないのう。\n"
"いつも感謝してるぞい。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:84
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#84"
msgid ""
"物欲を利用しようというのですか・・・。\n"
"・・・なるほどね。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:85
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#85"
msgid ""
"やったー、おおきに、ありがとう。\n"
"ごっつ嬉しいなぁ。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:86
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#86"
msgid ""
"ズーズーズー！\n"
"ズーズズー！"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#. Same Japanese also at: COMBDATA/BOSSTALK.EVE#14, BUTU_SRF.MDT#15, BUTU_SRF.MDT#51, BUTU_SRF.MDT#123.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:87
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#87"
msgid "・・・・・・・・。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:108
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#108"
msgid "長イ、ツキアイニ、ナリソウダナ。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:109
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#109"
msgid ""
"キサマ、ヨクシテクレル。\n"
"ダカラ、オレサマ、カワル。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:110
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#110"
msgid ""
"年々歳々花相似、歳々年々人不同・・・。\n"
"然し、我は永遠の忠誠を誓うなり。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:111
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#111"
msgid ""
"貴殿と出会えたことを、感謝する。\n"
"感謝だけでは足りんかもな・・・。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:112
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#112"
msgid "今までつくしてくれたお礼をしたいわ。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:113
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#113"
msgid ""
"俺も恩義を知らないわけじゃねぇからな。\n"
"いいぜ、業魔殿に連れていけよ。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:114
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#114"
msgid ""
"ここまでされちゃ、アタシだって・・・、\n"
"私を業魔殿へ連れてって！"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:115
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#115"
msgid ""
"今度から、おじさんのこと、\n"
"お兄さんって呼ぶよ。いいだろ・・・。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:116
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#116"
msgid ""
"おじちゃん、あたしがいないと困る？\n"
"いつも、いっしょにいてあげるね。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:117
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#117"
msgid ""
"あなたの気持ちだけで十分なのに・・・。\n"
"アタシ、いつもあなたの側にいたい・・・。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
#. Limit: Battle window. Keep lines short; current English uses at most 24 letters per line in BTL_SRF
#. and 40 in BUTU_SRF.
#: BUTU_SRF.MDT:118
msgctxt "BUTU_SRF.MDT#118"
msgid ""
"オレとおまえは、ウッキーだ。\n"
"これからも、よきウッキーでいよう。"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Short lines spoken during battle by another group of characters (read the lines).
